WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.253 --> 00:00:02.836
(upbeat music)

00:00:16.380 --> 00:00:17.950
- [Man] Sarah Lynn, I've seen.

00:00:17.950 --> 00:00:18.783
- Really?

00:00:18.783 --> 00:00:20.550
- About a month before she died,

00:00:20.550 --> 00:00:22.110
it was pretty clear she was using.

00:00:22.110 --> 00:00:22.943
- Well, how do you figure?

00:00:22.943 --> 00:00:23.990
Did she say something?

00:00:23.990 --> 00:00:26.410
- She didn't, but her friend did.

00:00:26.410 --> 00:00:27.243
- Her friend?

00:00:27.243 --> 00:00:28.076
- Large fella.

00:00:28.076 --> 00:00:30.440
I think he was a horse or a bull maybe.

00:00:30.440 --> 00:00:31.320
It's hard to remember.

00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:33.410
Kinda like a rounder Brad Garret type

00:00:33.410 --> 00:00:35.250
but with a very forgettable face.

00:00:35.250 --> 00:00:37.450
He told a story though, I remember that.

00:00:37.450 --> 00:00:41.076
It was about a trip he took to New Mexico.

00:00:41.076 --> 00:00:41.930
- Oh?

00:00:41.930 --> 00:00:44.764
- Yeah, it was about a girl and a mother.

00:00:44.764 --> 00:00:47.030
Oh, this is so long ago now.

00:00:47.030 --> 00:00:48.960
I think he had sex with the girl

00:00:48.960 --> 00:00:50.750
or maybe he had sex with the mother.

00:00:50.750 --> 00:00:52.440
- Well, do get your story sorted.

00:00:52.440 --> 00:00:54.660
But I prefer it if it's sordid.

00:00:54.660 --> 00:00:56.300
- And this man left with Sarah Lynn?

00:00:56.300 --> 00:00:58.180
Do you recall anything
else about this man?

00:00:58.180 --> 00:00:59.470
His name, perhaps?

00:00:59.470 --> 00:01:01.870
- No, I remember the girl's name.

00:01:01.870 --> 00:01:03.480
- Yes, Sarah Lynn.

00:01:03.480 --> 00:01:04.830
Now we're all up to speed.

00:01:04.830 --> 00:01:08.540
- No, the girl from his
story, the one in Mexico.

00:01:08.540 --> 00:01:10.470
He was weirdly proud of it.

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:13.080
Said her name was Penny Carson.

00:01:13.080 --> 00:01:14.347
- Carson, eh?

00:01:14.347 --> 00:01:16.067
- "Penny Carson," he said.

00:01:16.067 --> 00:01:18.973
"And that's her real name,
you can look her up."

00:01:18.973 --> 00:01:22.547
I remember thinking, "Why does
he want us to look her up?"

00:01:23.605 --> 00:01:24.990
- [Paige And Maximillian] Hmm.

00:01:24.990 --> 00:01:26.830
- You know, I actually didn't even drink

00:01:26.830 --> 00:01:27.860
for like all of college.

00:01:27.860 --> 00:01:29.543
I had some shit go down in high school,

00:01:29.543 --> 00:01:31.810
there was this girl in my town.

00:01:31.810 --> 00:01:33.470
Anyways, it's a long story.

00:01:33.470 --> 00:01:35.020
- No, I wanna hear it.

00:01:35.020 --> 00:01:39.990
- Okay, she had this
man living in her house.

00:01:39.990 --> 00:01:41.890
- You mean like more than one dad?

00:01:41.890 --> 00:01:44.550
- No, no, she had just the one dad

00:01:44.550 --> 00:01:46.390
but then there was this other guy.

00:01:46.390 --> 00:01:47.223
- Weird.

00:01:47.223 --> 00:01:48.120
- Totally weird, right?

00:01:48.120 --> 00:01:50.500
Okay, so this girl was best
friends with my girlfriend.

00:01:50.500 --> 00:01:54.070
We all went to prom
together, me, my girlfriend,

00:01:54.070 --> 00:01:55.800
the girl and the man.

00:01:55.800 --> 00:01:58.101
- Wait, the man went to prom with you?

00:01:58.101 --> 00:01:58.934
Eesh.

00:01:58.934 --> 00:02:01.020
- That's not even the eeshiest part!

00:02:01.020 --> 00:02:02.430
This guy bought us bourbon

00:02:02.430 --> 00:02:04.580
and practically forced us to drink it,

00:02:04.580 --> 00:02:06.366
and then when my girlfriend
got alcohol poisoning

00:02:06.366 --> 00:02:09.040
he just ditched us at the ER.

00:02:09.040 --> 00:02:10.230
- Was your girlfriend okay?

00:02:10.230 --> 00:02:11.920
- Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:02:11.920 --> 00:02:13.460
I mean, it was scary in the moment.

00:02:13.460 --> 00:02:15.626
We were there all night
and they pumped her stomach

00:02:15.626 --> 00:02:17.746
and I was pretty traumatized for a while

00:02:17.746 --> 00:02:19.930
but things are good now, things are good

00:02:19.930 --> 00:02:23.170
because at some point I realized it wasn't

00:02:23.170 --> 00:02:26.920
the alcohol's fault or
Maddie's fault or my fault.

00:02:26.920 --> 00:02:28.540
It was just some shitty dude, you know.

00:02:28.540 --> 00:02:29.373
- Totally.

00:02:30.370 --> 00:02:32.212
- But you know the craziest part of all?

00:02:32.212 --> 00:02:36.550
The guy, he's actually kind of famous.

00:02:36.550 --> 00:02:37.420
- Really?

00:02:37.420 --> 00:02:38.253
- Yeah, I never heard of him

00:02:38.253 --> 00:02:40.893
but it turns out he's
kind of a movie star.

00:02:42.090 --> 00:02:43.376
- Who is he?

00:02:43.376 --> 00:02:45.543
(exhales)

00:02:49.670 --> 00:02:50.523
Who is he?

00:02:51.750 --> 00:02:52.583
- What are you doing?

00:02:52.583 --> 00:02:54.620
- I'm updating my asexual dating profile

00:02:54.620 --> 00:02:55.910
with some fresh pics.

00:02:55.910 --> 00:02:57.460
There's still no one else on the app,

00:02:57.460 --> 00:02:59.920
but when they join, I wanna be ready.

00:02:59.920 --> 00:03:03.853
Look at this busted photo,
it's from over a year ago.

00:03:05.750 --> 00:03:07.160
- Yeah, you gotta stay current.

00:03:07.160 --> 00:03:09.020
- Oh man, they always ask for your job.

00:03:09.020 --> 00:03:10.680
Oh, I actually have a job.

00:03:10.680 --> 00:03:12.700
Hypeman for babies.

00:03:12.700 --> 00:03:14.040
- Is it like a Jesus thing?

00:03:14.040 --> 00:03:15.860
- No, it's not that, I told you.

00:03:15.860 --> 00:03:19.293
- I'm just confused is all,
because I thought you liked me.

00:03:19.293 --> 00:03:21.679
- I do, but I was very clear
there are certain things

00:03:21.679 --> 00:03:23.580
that I'm not interested in.

00:03:23.580 --> 00:03:25.677
- So why did you go out
with me in the first place?

00:03:25.677 --> 00:03:27.200
- Because I like you.

00:03:27.200 --> 00:03:28.720
Look, it's complicated.

00:03:28.720 --> 00:03:30.310
- And you're sure it's not a Jesus thing?

00:03:30.310 --> 00:03:31.980
- Fine, if it helps end this conversation,

00:03:31.980 --> 00:03:33.290
yes, it's a Jesus thing.

00:03:33.290 --> 00:03:34.786
- Hey, I admire your devotion.

00:03:34.786 --> 00:03:36.430
What would Jesus do?

00:03:36.430 --> 00:03:37.313
Not this guy.

00:03:39.240 --> 00:03:40.680
- It's not a Jesus thing.

00:03:40.680 --> 00:03:41.630
- I figured.

00:03:41.630 --> 00:03:43.520
I don't wanna presume anything,

00:03:43.520 --> 00:03:45.650
but there's an app you
might be interested in.

00:03:45.650 --> 00:03:46.483
- An app?

00:03:49.113 --> 00:03:51.530
(Todd sighs)

00:03:53.238 --> 00:03:54.071
(phone dings)

00:03:54.071 --> 00:03:55.541
- Oh.

00:03:55.541 --> 00:03:56.374
Ah.

00:03:57.710 --> 00:03:59.360
- Your psychiatrist said you're depressed.

00:03:59.360 --> 00:04:01.046
- Okay, yeah, I've been a little depressed

00:04:01.046 --> 00:04:03.170
but I'm not like depressed.

00:04:03.170 --> 00:04:04.910
I don't have depression.

00:04:04.910 --> 00:04:06.410
- You're smoking three packs a day.

00:04:06.410 --> 00:04:08.660
You've been wearing the same
pajama bottoms for weeks.

00:04:08.660 --> 00:04:09.969
- This is all part of my writing process.

00:04:09.969 --> 00:04:12.240
My best stuff comes
out when I hate myself.

00:04:12.240 --> 00:04:13.073
- What stuff?

00:04:13.073 --> 00:04:14.542
No stuff is coming out.

00:04:14.542 --> 00:04:15.375
- Ugh.

00:04:16.670 --> 00:04:18.710
- I'd feel better if you just tried

00:04:18.710 --> 00:04:20.390
the medication your doctor prescribed.

00:04:20.390 --> 00:04:21.860
- Well, I'd feel worse.

00:04:21.860 --> 00:04:23.630
They put me on Prozac in college,

00:04:23.630 --> 00:04:24.950
and I was so calm and boring,

00:04:24.950 --> 00:04:26.770
I didn't even wanna LiveJournal.

00:04:26.770 --> 00:04:28.160
And then Dawson's Creek got bad

00:04:28.160 --> 00:04:30.140
because there was no one
to speak truth to power.

00:04:30.140 --> 00:04:32.043
- Dawson's Creek did not get bad.

00:04:32.043 --> 00:04:33.227
You just started taking antidepressants,

00:04:33.227 --> 00:04:34.992
which you should also do now.

00:04:34.992 --> 00:04:37.490
(gloomy music)

00:04:37.490 --> 00:04:39.030
- I think I'm depressed.

00:04:39.030 --> 00:04:39.863
- Yeah?

00:04:39.863 --> 00:04:42.150
- It started when I was
having trouble with my book.

00:04:42.150 --> 00:04:45.296
And then it kind of
snowballed into my boyfriend

00:04:45.296 --> 00:04:47.045
saying I should take antidepressants.

00:04:47.045 --> 00:04:48.480
- Are you going to?

00:04:48.480 --> 00:04:49.540
- What's the point?

00:04:49.540 --> 00:04:50.570
- Of antidepressants?

00:04:50.570 --> 00:04:52.610
I believe the point is
to be antidepressed.

00:04:52.610 --> 00:04:55.416
- Sure, or you just flip over the nothing

00:04:55.416 --> 00:04:58.620
and underneath there's more nothing.

00:04:58.620 --> 00:05:00.690
- [Hollyhock] They canceled
all the drama classes.

00:05:00.690 --> 00:05:01.880
- [BoJack] What, why?

00:05:01.880 --> 00:05:03.230
- The acting professor quit,

00:05:03.230 --> 00:05:05.720
he got cast in a regional commercial.

00:05:05.720 --> 00:05:06.890
- And he quit?

00:05:06.890 --> 00:05:07.723
Wow.

00:05:07.723 --> 00:05:10.070
- So yeah, now Tawnie's
gotta change her major,

00:05:10.070 --> 00:05:13.670
which, I get why that sucks,
but don't take it out on me.

00:05:13.670 --> 00:05:15.201
- I'll bet a lot of actors would love

00:05:15.201 --> 00:05:17.240
to teach in a place like this.

00:05:17.240 --> 00:05:18.830
They're not looking for a replacement?

00:05:18.830 --> 00:05:20.320
- Maybe they are, I don't know.

00:05:20.320 --> 00:05:22.634
What do I look like, the Wesleyan Argus?

00:05:22.634 --> 00:05:24.970
(phone ringing)

00:05:24.970 --> 00:05:25.803
- Hello?

00:05:25.803 --> 00:05:26.820
- Ugh, Raven's out.

00:05:26.820 --> 00:05:28.470
She taught a workshop at Spellman,

00:05:28.470 --> 00:05:30.840
and to quote Raven, "Never more!"

00:05:30.840 --> 00:05:33.832
Spring semester starts
next week, can you be here?

00:05:33.832 --> 00:05:35.656
(upbeat music)

00:05:35.656 --> 00:05:37.580
- I'll be on the next plane.

00:05:37.580 --> 00:05:39.873
- [Dean] Welcome to Wesleyan, Professor.

00:05:42.662 --> 00:05:43.495
- [Pickles] Lights up!

00:05:43.495 --> 00:05:45.380
- Pickles, wait, before
Robot House assaults us

00:05:45.380 --> 00:05:46.820
with the harsh unforgiving glare

00:05:46.820 --> 00:05:50.080
of our energy-efficient bulbs,
I need to tell you this.

00:05:50.080 --> 00:05:51.510
- But it's so dark in here.

00:05:51.510 --> 00:05:53.500
- What I'm about to
confess is so shameful,

00:05:53.500 --> 00:05:55.890
I can only admit it in
the cover of shadow.

00:05:55.890 --> 00:05:57.110
- Don't be silly.

00:05:57.110 --> 00:05:57.943
- Lights on!

00:05:57.943 --> 00:05:58.934
- I cheated on you!

00:05:58.934 --> 00:05:59.767
- [Crowd] Supri--

00:05:59.767 --> 00:06:01.630
- Did someone just say something?

00:06:01.630 --> 00:06:02.984
- Don't change the subject!

00:06:02.984 --> 00:06:05.150
You cheated on me?

00:06:05.150 --> 00:06:06.790
- I want us to stay together.

00:06:06.790 --> 00:06:08.049
I want you to trust me.

00:06:08.049 --> 00:06:11.470
I wanna make us even somehow.

00:06:11.470 --> 00:06:12.330
- Even?

00:06:12.330 --> 00:06:13.980
The only logical way to be even

00:06:13.980 --> 00:06:16.520
would be if I got to
sleep with somebody else.

00:06:16.520 --> 00:06:18.380
- Okay, if that's what needs to happen.

00:06:18.380 --> 00:06:19.213
- Really?

00:06:19.213 --> 00:06:20.950
- Yeah, we just have to think who--

00:06:20.950 --> 00:06:22.238
- Buzzy, my high school boyfriend Buzzy.

00:06:22.238 --> 00:06:24.150
- Very quick at that name, but okay, fine.

00:06:24.150 --> 00:06:26.200
- No, you don't even know him.

00:06:26.200 --> 00:06:27.970
Knowing is what hurts the most.

00:06:27.970 --> 00:06:32.260
What if I sleep with Buzzy
and Tyler from SoulCycle?

00:06:32.260 --> 00:06:34.240
I thought it'd be easy to get even,

00:06:34.240 --> 00:06:36.950
but I've slept with 32 guys now

00:06:36.950 --> 00:06:38.500
if you count the two sets of twins

00:06:38.500 --> 00:06:39.740
as two and not four.

00:06:39.740 --> 00:06:40.573
- I do.

00:06:40.573 --> 00:06:43.610
- And the truth is, none
of them are like my mister.

00:06:43.610 --> 00:06:46.923
I just wish I could cheat on you with you.

00:06:48.275 --> 00:06:49.233
- Hmm?

00:06:49.233 --> 00:06:50.340
(door slams)

00:06:50.340 --> 00:06:51.730
(laughing)

00:06:51.730 --> 00:06:53.193
- Hanging in there.

00:06:55.290 --> 00:06:57.778
- I think I may have an idea.

00:06:57.778 --> 00:07:00.883
♪ There was no sunlight ♪

00:07:00.883 --> 00:07:04.050
♪ Just ask my mother ♪

